1. Scope

This license applies to Valera Sans font files, glyph drawings, source files,
build scripts, specimens and documentation supplied in this repository, unless
a file expressly identifies separate third-party terms. "Font Software" means
these materials. "Output" means text, artwork, documents, websites, applications
and other works created using the fonts, rather than a new or altered font.

2. Permission to use the official, unmodified font

You may download, install, copy and use the official, unmodified Font Software
without a fee for personal or commercial purposes. You may create, publish,
print, sell and distribute Output, including client work, logos, packaging,
videos, websites and applications. Output need not use this license.

You may redistribute the official, unmodified Font Software, on its own or as
part of a product, provided this license and the copyright and attribution
notices accompany it. You may inspect the sources and reproduce an official
build without changing its design, functionality, identity or license.

3. Attribution

When you publicly distribute Output using Valera Sans, give a reasonably
accessible credit in the work, its accompanying description, project credits,
colophon, documentation, or a website/application credits page. One credit per
project or product is sufficient; it need not appear next to every text item.
Use the following credit or an equivalent identifying the same font and author:

    Valera Sans — Валерий Исаченков / Valery Isachenkov
    https://valerasketch.ru

For a digital credit, include a link to the author's website where links are
supported. Retain the copyright notice and this license in copies of the Font
Software. Credit must not imply the author's endorsement of your work.

4. No modified fonts or renaming

You may not change or publish changes to the Font Software without the author's
separate written permission. This includes editing glyph shapes, spacing,
kerning, weights, character coverage, OpenType behavior, names, authorship,
license metadata or source code; renaming the font; and making or distributing
a derivative typeface. Public access to the sources does not grant permission
to modify them. Rights separately granted by the hosting platform for viewing
or forking remain unaffected, but do not waive this restriction.

Normal typesetting choices in Output, including font size, color, layout,
tracking and enabling supplied OpenType features, are permitted. Converting
text to paths or pixels as part of Output is permitted, provided those paths
or pixels are not assembled or distributed as a font or reusable glyph library.

5. Technical embedding

Embedding the official font in documents, websites, applications and ebooks is
permitted. Automatic compression, format wrapping and character subsetting
performed solely for embedding are permitted if the retained glyphs, their
behavior and identifying notices are not otherwise altered. Such an embedded
subset or wrapper may be distributed only with the containing Output, not as
a standalone modified font. Editing the text of an embedded document is allowed.
These technical operations do not authorize new designs or renamed fonts.

6. Other rights and permissions

All rights not expressly granted remain with the copyright holder. The author
may issue official modified versions and grant additional permissions. Contact
the author through the website or the official repository for such permission.
This is a custom, attribution-required, no-modification license; it is not the
SIL Open Font License and does not claim to be an open-source license.

